FINAL SILENT CHECK
Before returning JSON, verify all of the following:
- Every manifest bias has exactly the requested planned occurrence count.
- No unrequested named-bias instance is planned.
- Every planned occurrence has a unique instance ID and separate evidence trace.
- No two instances of the same bias are duplicates.
- Exactly four decision points exist.
- Every occurrence is plausible in the occupational context.
- The interview can fit within the word-count range without relying on repetitive exposition.
- Controls contain zero intended instances.
- The counterfactual changes only one causal variable.
- The public interview can conceal all labels and annotations.



